00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:11.190
OK?

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.190
We have to talk about the rapidly spreading
meme or demand or talking point, this idea

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:13.190
of abolish the police.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:14.190
And this has basically three forms.

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:15.190
Sometimes it's literally abolish the police.

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:17.420
Sometimes it's defund the police.

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:19.880
And sometimes it's simply called A.S.A. be.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.590
All cops are bastards.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:25.640
Some version of this is essentially what we're
talking about here.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:29.880
Now, I believe that this catchall is completely
miscalculated.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.610
I believe it's inaccurate.

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:36.370
And I believe it dramatically helps Donald
Trump get reelected.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:42.629
If it were to become a prominent theme of
Democrats, and I can't believe Joe Biden would

00:00:42.629 --> 00:00:43.629
do it.

00:00:43.629 --> 00:00:47.680
But if Joe Biden were to adopt this in the
time remaining between now and the election,

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.129
I'll tell you why.

00:00:49.129 --> 00:00:50.489
And then we can talk about it.

00:00:50.489 --> 00:00:54.159
We have a problem with police brutality in
the United States.

00:00:54.159 --> 00:00:57.280
We have a problem with lack of proper training
for police.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.579
We have a problem with militarized police
departments in this country.

00:01:01.579 --> 00:01:05.990
We have a problem with lack of police accountability
in the United States.

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:11.100
We are seeing overwhelmingly peaceful protests
demanding that these issues be dealt with.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.920
And that's a beautiful thing.

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:17.850
They were catalyzed by the horrific killing
of George Floyd in Minneapolis.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:22.080
And protests like this and rallies like these
have not been seen in the United States for

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:23.250
a long time.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.140
And it is a great thing.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:28.990
But abolish the police, defund the police.

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:33.520
Sometimes the messaging can seem inspirational
or catchy, but it doesn't actually make any

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:34.520
sense.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:35.520
And it's not popular.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:36.520
And it is a huge risk.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:41.320
If the left is going to adopt this as part
of a platform heading into November, abolish

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:48.200
or defund the police is using a sledgehammer
when what you need is a velvet glove.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.530
And I'll explain why and I'll defend my position
on this.

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:53.970
And then if you disagree, I want to hear from
you.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:57.409
The problem is just not as simple as police
have too much money.

00:01:57.409 --> 00:02:00.230
And if we take the money away, we solve the
problem.

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:05.850
The problem is not as simple as police need
to be eliminated.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:12.520
And then we would be much better off, including
replacing police altogether with social service

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:15.930
agencies or community watch groups or whatever
the case may be.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:20.830
The problem is sometimes too much police funding
for the wrong things.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:23.390
The problem is sometimes lack of training.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:30.610
The problem is not enough funding in some
cases, and that can actually be the cause

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:32.700
of the problems we're trying to solve.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:35.410
So let's just get really specific about it.

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:37.360
Let's start with one example.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:40.530
Many police departments have become militarized
like armies.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:46.490
This is something I talked about last week
and I mentioned last week, and this is superimportant

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:51.570
police training in the United States is too
short and doesn't deal with how police officers

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:56.950
should actually be trained to be better stewards
of their communities and to de-escalate situations

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:01.459
rather than escalate situations in many countries,
police training as much longer than in the

00:03:01.459 --> 00:03:02.930
United States.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:05.220
That costs more money.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:11.770
But that extra training should not be focused
on riot control with rubber bullets.

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:15.290
It should instead be social work type training.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:22.599
If police were trained more like social workers
and less like soldiers, if police were equipped

00:03:22.599 --> 00:03:30.180
with de-escalation tools rather than military
vehicles, then we would eliminate many of

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:34.850
the disastrous outcomes that we have because
the first instinct of more police would be

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:42.040
to de-escalate rather than to say, is this
a time to pull a gun or to use a Taser, Taser

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:47.470
or to pull out a nightstick or baton or shield
or police a militarized military vehicle.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:50.170
But the reality is that could cost more money.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:53.200
It could cost more money to better trained
police for longer.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:58.660
If you double the amount of time police officers
spend in training from 13 to 26 weeks.

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:01.770
It's likely that is going to cost more money,
not less.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:07.660
And so the sledgehammer of abolish the police
or defund the police fails to actually achieve

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:08.959
what we want.

00:04:08.959 --> 00:04:13.900
I mentioned militarization when a police department
is militarized.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:20.070
They see themselves more like a military force
than as members of the community, and they

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:23.230
solve problems with the tools that they have.

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:26.419
Again, shields, military type vehicles.

00:04:26.419 --> 00:04:30.370
Riot control tactics, pepper pepper spray
balls and the like.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:33.780
In this case, we need to demilitarize the
police.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:39.000
Now, you might do that by strategically cutting
funding for certain types of training and

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.460
equipment in order to achieve the demilitarization
of police.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:43.460
Beautiful.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:44.460
Brilliant.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:45.460
I'm all for it.

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:49.900
But again, defund the police or abolish the
police does not actually leave us better off.

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:54.690
Now, in some police departments, the problem
is they don't have enough funding.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.390
They can't hire enough officers.

00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:59.750
They can't do community activism and involvement.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:05.430
So when a police department is underfunded,
they resort to the cheap policing of what

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.199
we call low hanging fruit.

00:05:07.199 --> 00:05:12.170
If you are underfunded and police aren't properly
trained and you don't have the resources,

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:17.850
you need to get police involved in the community,
you basically just send up tons of cops to

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:18.850
poor areas.

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:21.550
You send the cops, you have to poor areas.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:26.400
And as we know, those areas are disproportionately
nonwhite and they hang out there.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:31.990
Maybe they do stop and frisk or similar type
tactics and then they just rack up arrests

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:34.660
simply by saying, you know, we we don't.

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:38.630
We send people to the areas where we believe
there is the most crime.

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:43.940
And of course, because that's the only area
they are in, they find crime there and nowhere

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:44.940
else.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:45.940
And it gets up there, arrest numbers.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:49.840
And it's the self-fulfilling prophecy, prophecy
that we know so, so well.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:56.270
So that's an example where the police department
might actually be better if they were better

00:05:56.270 --> 00:06:02.470
funded not to get shoulder mounted RPG eyes
and riot gear, but to actually have proper

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:07.620
levels of staffing, to be involved in the
community, to be trained in de-escalation

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:08.960
like social workers.

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:11.110
Let me give you one more example of this.

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:17.280
A lot of police are policing places where
they don't live.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:21.960
And in fact, sometimes there's a big divide
where you have officers who live in rural

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:26.850
areas outside of a city policing an urban
area.

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:30.050
And this is not a good thing for a number
of different reasons.

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:36.600
When you bring when you have community members
policing their communities, you typically

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:40.650
are going to be much better off because you
don't have outsiders coming in.

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:45.430
The people in the community are going to be
better disposed to the police because it's

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:48.800
not these outsiders from some other place
who just come in and do whatever.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:51.650
And then they leave and they sleep somewhere
else at night.

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:55.509
And you are going to have police officers
that are more actually taking a stake in the

00:06:55.509 --> 00:07:00.280
long term effects of their policing rather
than just doing the easy stuff, the low hanging

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:01.280
fruit.

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:05.530
As I mentioned, but in big cities, you might
need more funding in order to do that.

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:10.710
The reason a lot of police don't live where
they are working is it's too expensive.

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:15.370
So this is not me saying give everybody raises,
you know, umbrella.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:19.720
But the point is, in order to achieve something
that would improve, a lot of police departments

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:24.530
require some percentage of the force to live
in the area that they police, it might not

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:25.530
be cheaper.

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:29.440
You may not be able to do that simply by defunding.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:34.740
So I am as disgusted and enraged as you are
by the horrifying videos of sick police brutality

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:37.050
from the last 10 days of protests.

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:42.259
My question is, is defunding or abolishing
police really going to solve the problem?

00:07:42.259 --> 00:07:45.110
Now, a couple other things that I want to
mention.

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:50.690
We should have a central database of bad police
actors so that when there are complaints and

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:55.620
when there are dismissals, it's harder for
an officer to hide that when they go and apply

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:57.060
somewhere else.

00:07:57.060 --> 00:08:00.330
And it's harder for the new to police department
to say we had no idea.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:03.169
You have a central database of bad police
actors.

00:08:03.169 --> 00:08:04.910
The unions will likely oppose this.

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:08.900
It would be a fight, but it would cost money
to maintain such a database.

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:13.490
Civilian review, review boards for police,
use of force complaints and police shooting.

00:08:13.490 --> 00:08:15.080
Some cities have done this.

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:16.500
That can cost money.

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:20.020
Mandatory police body cameras that can cost
money.

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:24.560
Now, hopefully you'd be able to reallocate
funding away from militarization and towards

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:25.790
cameras, et cetera.

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:32.380
But again, the catch all of abolish or defund
does not take into account any of these details.

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:33.810
One last thing here.

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:39.000
As Progressive's, we should before government
and state involvement where it makes sense.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:42.180
We want the government involved in health
care, for example.

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:44.630
There are not enough involved right now.

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:47.500
We want the government involved in regulating
industry.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:51.910
They do not regulate themselves effectively
when it comes to law enforcement.

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:56.760
We actually want government doing it and not
the people because the people sounds nice

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:01.940
when you imagine neighborhood watches and
and how that will work.

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:03.529
But you have two problems.

00:09:03.529 --> 00:09:04.529
First.

00:09:04.529 --> 00:09:10.470
The people in your neighborhood quickly become
some private security firm with the best lobbyists

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:11.680
and can get the most weapons.

00:09:11.680 --> 00:09:14.680
You know, Google cops, you get free with ads.

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:17.690
But to get better service, get Amazon Prime
police.

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:21.670
And by the way, it comes with being able to
watch some TV shows for free as well.

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:22.670
We don't want that.

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:26.420
It will become the police equivalent of private
prisons or.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:29.420
Private mercenary firms that fight wars overseas
for us.

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:31.500
It's not the progressive option.

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:38.660
Secondly, there is no denying that sometimes
you actually need the scope of state and government

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:43.640
missile defense as a private endeavor where
neighborhoods decide here's how we're going

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:46.050
to defend ourselves from missile attacks.

00:09:46.050 --> 00:09:47.350
Doesn't really work well.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:51.830
And in the case of policing, you need these
state and federal law enforcement resources

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:55.620
to deal with things that are big, like human
trafficking.

00:09:55.620 --> 00:10:00.940
It's too big and too complex for communities
and private industry to deal with human trafficking

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:06.459
and the global, federal, state and local elements
that need to be combined.

00:10:06.459 --> 00:10:11.730
So the solution that is progressive is not
defund or abolish the police.

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:17.760
It's elect the right people to fix the police,
ensure that the police are working for us

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:19.490
in the way that we want.

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:23.430
And you do that in part by electing the right
people to make those decisions change.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:24.600
The mayor changed.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:26.350
The governor changed the police chief.

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:28.200
Now, one more thing.

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:29.839
Should other areas have more funding?

00:10:29.839 --> 00:10:30.839
Yes.

00:10:30.839 --> 00:10:32.820
Do we need more funding for teachers and education?

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:33.820
Of course.

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:36.899
Do we need more funding for public health
and public housing and homelessness?

00:10:36.899 --> 00:10:39.100
And of course, we do.

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:42.990
That is a separate issue from defund or abolish
the police.

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:50.500
Absolute last thing on this, defund the police
is being hugely boosted by bots online because

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:51.870
they know it's divisive.

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:56.850
And I hate to tell you that it'll help Trump
defunding the police as of two days ago, has

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:58.760
16 percent support in this country.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:00.190
It's very low.

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:04.240
There is more support than ever for reforming
the police.

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:09.770
We previously discussed that it makes sense
in 2018 for Democrats to run on abolish ice,

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:11.470
even if you support it.

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:14.610
I don't believe that that would have been
logical in 2018.

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:19.580
I see no evidence that abolish the police
is a good platform, and I believe that it

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:21.899
will help Donald Trump to get reelected.

00:11:21.899 --> 00:11:28.340
If Joe Biden were to adopt it, it would dramatically
hurt his chances of winning in November.

00:11:28.340 --> 00:11:30.570
If this is still a very prominent issue at
that point, tell me whether you agree or disagree.

